<title>USA: Leslie-ADM soybean production survey by state.</title>
<headline>Leslie-ADM soybean production survey by state.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following tables contain state-by-state soybean production estimates published in the Leslie-ADM Investor Services Crop survey.</p>
<p>U.S. SOYBEAN PRODUCTION (IN 000'S BUSHELS)</p>
<p>	 LESLIE 11/1/96 USDA 10/1/96  USDA 1995</p>
<p> PENN	   12,825	12,540	 9,450</p>
<p> OHIO	  145,925     152,660     153,140</p>
<p> INDIANA     209,040     203,680     196,710</p>
<p> ILLINOIS    398,925     384,150     378,300</p>
<p> MICHIGAN     50,840	52,480	59,600</p>
<p> WISCONSIN    30,450	32,190	34,400</p>
<p> MINN	  218,300     218,300     234,900</p>
<p> IOWA	  425,250     415,800     407,440</p>
<p> MISSOURI    153,900     145,800     132,750</p>
<p> N DAKOTA     23,780	23,780	18,560</p>
<p> S DAKOTA     90,100	90,100	75,000</p>
<p> NEBRASKA    138,460     135,450     100,980</p>
<p> KANSAS	 74,000	68,000	51,250</p>
<p> MARYLAND     15,840	15,840	11,730</p>
<p> VIRGINIA     15,840	15,840	11,280</p>
<p> N CAROLINA   34,800	34,800	26,750</p>
<p> S CAROLINA   14,040	14,040	12,720</p>
<p> GEORGIA	10,140	10,140	 8,370</p>
<p> KENTUCKY     43,660	43,660	41,400</p>
<p> TENNESSEE    40,250	40,250	34,560</p>
<p> ALABAMA	 9,135	 9,135	 5,400</p>
<p> MISS	   50,750	50,750	37,800</p>
<p> ARKANSAS    115,200     115,200	88,400</p>
<p> LOUISIANA    35,175	34,650	26,000</p>
<p> TEXAS	   7,830	 7,830	 6,000</p>
<p> OTHERS	 19,282	19,155	13,924</p>
<p> TOTAL     2,383,737   2,346,220   2,176,814</p>
